trying to get your kid into a Harvard or  Yale there's an algorithm for that and  it measures their true odds  parents are obsessed with getting their  kids into the best colleges like NYU and  these same schools are obsessed with  keeping their top rankings in part by  attracting lots of applicants after all  a growing denominator with a fixed  numerator creates shrinking percentages  reflecting slim acceptance rates and  enticing exclusivity it's no wonder the  college application process feels rigged  think of the costs involved both in  money and time prepping for multiple AP  exams year-round travel Sports  extracurriculars campus visits private  College counseling application fees and  for what schools like to talk up their  holistic admissions process where they  carefully weigh each student's unique  attributes alongside conventional  academic credentials when the truth is  it's a black box  so a couple of c-suite Executives took  action they formed a non-profit called  transparency in admissions using the  piles of data Harvard was forced to  disclose in a lawsuit over its race  conscious admissions policies the team  extrapolated those results to other top  schools to determine the probabilities  of admission for different populations  as frustrated parents themselves the  executives say their goal is to save  other families anxiety and money by  providing a snapshot of students true  odds here's how students take an online  survey input details like ethnicity  household income grades they pay up to  25 and in return receive a list of  acceptance probabilities at the top  schools based on their individual  profile  bottom line you have a bit of an edge if  say you're recruited athlete or a child  of big donors or first generation  college student by and large the data  show that huge Slots of students have  almost zero chance of getting into the  most elite schools now this is something  you might have suspected before you  began this journey but now you have the  data to back it up
 

